+  // Flattening memory -- everything in one segment at offset 0 -- is what lets
+  // the memory image be written back when we are done. MemoryUtils::flatten
+  // refuses a module with a passive segment, and one where any expression
+  // names a segment; array.new_data is such an expression, and it is how a GC
+  // language materialises a constant array, so for those modules flattening
+  // never succeeds.
+  //
